cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the associated paper and this software bundle."
title: "1+3 covariant CMB anisotropies: analytical reproducibility software"
type: software
# Tracks the tag that exists, not the one being prepared. GitHub's "Cite this
# repository" reads this field, so a version here that has not been released
# asserts a release that cannot be fetched.
version: "1.2.0"
# Stamped by scripts/bump_release.py together with the version above, so the
# two cannot disagree about which release this file describes.
date-released: 2026-10-16
authors:
  - family-names: Gebbie
    given-names: Tim
doi: "10.25375/uct.34069509"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An independent Python reconstruction, from first 1+3 covariant principles, of
  the almost-Friedmann-Lemaitre results of Gebbie, Dunsby & Ellis, Annals of
  Physics 282, 321 (2000). Analytical release; no empirical data are required.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  # Decision S17, as amended 2026-10-20 (finding T-84): the title reads
  # `CMBR`, confirmed by the PI 2026-10-21 as the paper's own title. The
  # withdrawn Zenodo record is how the discrepancy was found, not what
  # settles it; a citation reproduces the title the paper carries.
  title: "Frame covariance of CMBR lensing in the exact 1+3 covariant radiation hierarchy"
  authors:
    - family-names: Gebbie
      given-names: Tim
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4061-2621"
      affiliation: "University of Cape Town"
  year: 2026
  month: 10
  # **Filled 2026-10-22 from the record that exists**, which is what S47 said
  # would happen at manuscript freeze. The `url` carries the VERSION SUFFIX
  # deliberately: a bare astro-ph/9912072 resolves to whatever is current, and
  # that identifier has carried three distinct documents -- v1/v2 the legacy
  # 1999 work, v3 THE CORRECTION, v4 Paper 1. The DOI is version-agnostic by arXiv's own
  # design, so the url is what pins it.
  doi: "10.48550/arXiv.astro-ph/9912072"
  url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/astro-ph/9912072v4"
  version: "v4"
  license: CC-BY-4.0
  notes: "Paper 1, arXiv:astro-ph/9912072v4, submitted to General Relativity and Gravitation 2026-10-16. CITE IT VERSIONED: v4 is Paper 1, v3 is the correction, v1/v2 are the legacy 1999 work."
keywords:
  - cosmic microwave background
  - 1+3 covariant formalism
  - multipole hierarchy
  - reproducibility
  - CMB lensing
  - frame covariance
